0012:     rotation_patch: rows h-3 to h-1; 3x3 with color-7 clock-hand (2 pixels from center toward up/right/down/left = 0/90/180/270 deg)
0013:   canvas:
0014:     width: grid_w minus legend+separator cols; height: grid_h
0015:     background: 2-4 non-{0,6} colors in bands/grid/nested-rings pattern [observed: usually 2 colors in uniform horizontal or vertical stripes]
0016:     constraint: canvas bg colors must be disjoint from unit sprite colors (both panels)
0017:   composite:
0018:     build: tile color-swapped unit into each active frame cell -> (fh*uh) x (fw*uw)
0019:     rotate: rot90 by -k (k from rotation patch)
0020:     place: anchor_to_topleft maps (pr,pc) to canvas offset; composite must fit fully (no clipping)
0021:     overlay: non-{0,6} composite pixels overwrite canvas; canvas color-6 pixels preserved; when multiple composites exist, they must not overlap (no shared non-{0,6} pixels)
0022: 
0023: generation_strategy:
0024:   approach: output-first
0025:   steps:
0026:     1. Choose grid_h in 20-30, grid_w=30, num_legends in {1,2}.
0027:     2. Per legend, pick unit_size N in 2-5; legend_w = N+2. Compute canvas_w = grid_w - legend widths - separator widths.
0028:     3. Per legend, design unit_sprite (NxN, 2 colors, fully filled), frame mask (H x W, single color, 8-connected, active cells = 50-65% of H*W), anchor (pr,pc) in {0,1,2}^2, rotation k in {0,1,2,3}.
0029:     4. Compute rotated composite size; ensure it fits within canvas_h x canvas_w at chosen anchor. For 2 legends, ensure composites don't overlap. Reject/resample if not.
0030:     5. Build canvas background with 2 colors in horizontal or vertical bands (band width >= 4).
0031:     6. Build output by overlaying each rotated composite at its anchor position.
0032:     7. Build input by placing unmodified canvas (no overlay) into the grid, adding legend columns with unit sprite (color-swapped back), frame, marker square, and rotation patch, separated by all-6 columns.
0033:     8. Validate via solver.

